==Strategy==
Although this stage may appear intimidating with its multitude of strong peons, the stage provides plenty of time for the player to prepare for their arrival and their spawn rate is few and far between. The strong peon waves (containing Ginger Snaches, Gabriels, Doge Darks, and Brollows) spawn every 60 seconds until the two minute mark, with Trolly Bloggers and Bannerman Doges plugging the gaps. Players will find themselves pushed towards their base during these waves, but can take full advantage of the lulls to damage the boss. Units with low damage per hit are not recommended, as they will cause the peons to constantly rebound.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - [[Massive Damage]] versus Floating and fast speed makes Fishman a phenomenal counter to Nobunaga, able to score huge amounts of damage with relative ease. During the peon waves, he is also able to cripple if not outright kill any Brollow he can land a hit on. With lower-level cats or higher crown difficulties, however, do be careful of timing, as Fishman can easily be obliterated by Nobunaga's attacks,
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - [[Resistant]] versus Floating and a great health pool makes Octopus Cat the optimal method of stalling Nobunaga. Their occasional [[Weaken]] can also help greatly with other units' abilities being able to land hits on the boss. Do be careful with their usage when other peons are alive, as they can quickly perish upon sustaining consistent damage from the enemies that they don't target.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat/Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - Slime can heavily cripple any peon in the stage, as well as consistently chip down Nobunaga. If a level 30 Slime can successfully land a hit on any enemy, they can easily wipe all Brollows from the field, leaving all other peons on dangerously low health or outright dead (with higher levels). If one has obtained their True Form, this feat becomes even easier, as their improved range and [[Wave Attack|Wave]] range allows for greater destruction. Beware of other units making your Slime miss its attack.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle/Cats in the Stroller]] - Imagine Slime, but as a sustainable Uber. That's how Cats in the Cradle behaves here, except somehow even better. Although their [[Knockback]] won't be of any use here, their powerful damage, [[Immune to Freeze|Immunity to Freeze]], gargantuan health pool, and powerful Wave Attacks make them a great option for dealing with every single enemy of this stage. Their recharge also aligns with peon cycles near perfectly, meaning as long as they land their attack they'll be able to dish out enormous damage and dispatch most of the enemies on the field. Ultra Form only makes this easier, as their newly-gained [[Omni Strike]] ensures they miss much less.

==Trivia==
*Since it contains [[Revolutionary Nobunaga]], Despot's Ambition may be a reference to the ''[[wikipedia:Nobunaga's Ambition|Nobunaga's Ambition]]'' series of games.
*The [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Angel Enemies]] supporting Revolutionary Nobunaga may be a reference to how the real [[wikipedia:Oda Nobunaga|Oda Nobunaga]] is sometimes referred to as the "Demon King of the Sixth Heaven".

